@startuml
title ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema — the one navigation map, generated from source at build

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ClassBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
hide circle

entity "REGISTRY" as REG {
  version : string
  --
  instance.build  : int
  instance.commit : string
  instance.env    : local | dev | qa | prod
  instance.live   : bool
}

entity "TOOL" as TOOL {
  tool_name : string  <<key>>
  --
  tool_type : tool | pseudo_tool
  class_name / source_location
  description  <<TOOL_DESCRIPTION>>
  utterance_manager_prompt
}

entity "PAGE" as PAGE {
  page_name : string  <<key>>
  --
  subject : individualProvider |
  \tfacility | clinicalTrial
  description
  members : [tool_name]
  required_members : [tool_name] (subset)
  --
  completeness.render_timeout_seconds
  completeness.on_timeout   (layman prose)
  completeness.on_conflict         = raise
  completeness.on_missing_required = raise
}

entity "FIELD" as FIELD {
  name : string
  --
  type : string
  required : bool
  io : input | output
  description
}

entity "ROUTE" as ROUTE {
  route_name : string  <<key>>
  --
  call_type : one of five
}

entity "PROOF" as PROOF {
  method : none | api_key |
  \tsession_token | our_signature
  --
  credential_name   (api_key)
  signing_key_name  (our_signature)
}

entity "TIMEOUT_FACTS" as TF {
  render_timeout_seconds
  callback_timeout_seconds
  external_call_timeout_seconds
}

REG   ||--o{ TOOL
REG   ||--o{ ROUTE
REG   ||--o{ PAGE
PAGE  }o--o{ TOOL  : members
TOOL  ||--o{ FIELD
TOOL  ||--o{ TOOL  : may_call
TOOL  }o--o{ ROUTE : subscribes
ROUTE ||--|| PROOF
ROUTE ||--o| TF

note top of REG
  ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema. One record, generated
  from source at build, so it cannot name a tool, route or
  page the build does not carry. It combines the artifacts
  that carried the map: the tool contracts, the _OP_HANDLERS
  dispatch table, the ToolRouter allowlist, the UtteranceManager
  prompt, and the page composition. One document per build per
  environment; exactly one live per env; the deploy retires the
  predecessor's live flag — the only field ever mutated on an
  existing document.
end note

note right of TOOL
  Presence IS the allowlist. Every tool declares
  UTTERANCE_MANAGER_PROMPT or NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE —
  silence refuses the build. The gateway enters as a
  pseudo_tool. On the utterance_manager's own entry the
  prompt is the preamble, not a fragment.
end note

note bottom of FIELD
  required inputs are the prerequisites: the
  UniversalNavigator's completeness test compares
  the passed document against them before dispatch.
end note

note left of TOOL
  may_call IS the who-may-call-whom map.
  The generator refuses a circle — a DAG.
end note

note bottom of ROUTE
  subscriptions ARE the dispatch table: a call routes
  only to a tool subscribed to it. call_type is one of
  tool_to_tool, third_party_callback, static_witness,
  client_sessioned, internal_callback — each proof method
  fixed by its type.
end note

note right of PAGE
  THREE pages only. A detail view, the NUCC/specialty
  filter and Geo are page-scoped MEMBERS, never pages.
    individualProvider — required: ProviderSearch;
      members: SpecialtyFilter, ProviderDetail,
      ProviderSelection, Geo
    facility — required: FacilitySearch; members:
      facility NUCC filter (Ambulatory / Psychiatric /
      Inpatient, mirroring individual Prescribers/
      Homeopathic), FacilityDetail, Geo
    clinicalTrial — required: ClinicalTrials; members: Geo
  Geo runs parallel to the specialty/NUCC filter on
  individualProvider + facility (resolves free-text,
  misspelled geography).

  What a page MUST declare: members / required_members
  (a subset) / completeness. members name declared tools;
  required_members are the render-ledger expectation;
  the render ledger reconciles the page when every
  required_member closes OR render_timeout_seconds expires,
  and a page-merge conflict or a dead required member
  raises and is instrumented.

  THE GAP: the live build's registry instance predates the
  facility NUCC filter member, so a page's declared
  membership is only ever as complete as the build that
  generated it — the facility filter is current-iteration
  but not yet emitted by the generator.
end note
@enduml
